\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Scale-aware decomposition for the nine-variable model at $3$\,h lead. (a) system-size distribution, truth vs prediction; (b) precipitation carried by each scale; (c) POD and FAR vs scale; (d) median area ($\Delta \ln A$) and intensity ($\Delta \ln \rho $) bias vs scale; (e) precipitation-bias budget (area vs intensity share, plus missed/spurious fractions); (f) intensity distribution. Detection of small systems is near zero; their error budget is dominated by missed precipitation, not by distortion of correctly located systems.}}{8}{figure.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:scale}{{4}{8}{Scale-aware decomposition for the nine-variable model at $3$\,h lead. (a) system-size distribution, truth vs prediction; (b) precipitation carried by each scale; (c) POD and FAR vs scale; (d) median area ($\Delta \ln A$) and intensity ($\Delta \ln \rho $) bias vs scale; (e) precipitation-bias budget (area vs intensity share, plus missed/spurious fractions); (f) intensity distribution. Detection of small systems is near zero; their error budget is dominated by missed precipitation, not by distortion of correctly located systems}{figure.caption.10}{}}
